# UI Design System Theme Lock

- Use `AppShell` for authenticated routes and `FeaturePage` + `FeatureHeader` for feature-level pages.
- Dashboard dark green is the only primary brand color. Use Tailwind theme tokens from `tailwind.config.js`, especially `brand.primary`, instead of raw hex values.
- Do not add raw colors in components: no hex colors, arbitrary Tailwind color values like `bg-[#...]`, or feature-specific custom palettes.
- Do not force every card or module tile to use the brand color. Brand green is for headers, primary actions, accents, active states, and selected highlights.
- Use semantic shared components for new feature UI: `Button`, `FeatureCard`, `StatusAlert`, `LoadingState`, `EmptyState`, and `ActionMenu`.
- Feature modules must not define their own color systems. Use shared semantic variants such as `default`, `info`, `warning`, `danger`, `success`, `primary`, `secondary`, and `ghost`.
- Back navigation belongs in `FeatureHeader` top-left. Page-level primary actions belong in `FeatureHeader` top-right.
- Notification/profile header icons and dashboard greeting are approved primary brand usages.
